    "rss_method": "At each 25 ms sample, sum RSS of every process in the application session/process group, its descendant closure and the persistent reparented-descendant registry; report the maximum simultaneous total.",
    "pss_method": "Sum /proc/<pid>/smaps_rollup Pss for the same tracked set at PSS samples.",
    "cpu_method": "CPU totals excluded: the original tracker maximized the cumulative CPU of currently live processes instead of summing CPU across exited helpers. It could report zero child CPU despite observed Chromium. The harness is fixed for future runs; no corrected total can be recovered from this recorded artifact.",
    "helper_counting": "All browser renderer/gpu/network helpers are classified as browser and counted. The frozen yt-dlp PyInstaller binary runs as two processes with the same yt-dlp executable name (bootloader plus embedded CPython); both are counted as yt_dlp, so the embedded interpreter is represented by that count rather than a separate python-named process. yt-dlp's ffmpeg/ffprobe and qjs sidecars are counted as media/quickjs. Counts are maximum simultaneous processes per phase category, and the final cleanup samples expose any post-shutdown residue.",
    "argv_collected": false
  },
  "method": {
    "application": "real :desktopApp JVM, real Compose/AWT Window, real DesktopMusicServices",
    "window": "waited for a visible/showing AWT Window, then 10 s settle before auth verification",
    "offscreen": "private Xvfb display, 1440x900x24, software Skia; host DBUS preserved",
    "isolation": "Each run uses a disposable HOME/ARCHIVETUNE_HOME/XDG/TMPDIR and a Secret Service entry keyed by that run's data/youtube-session.dpapi path. The live keyring entry is read only and the live browser profile is never copied or opened.",
    "instrumentation": "Identical temporary Main.kt hook in disposable detached checkouts; delegated DesktopSessionProvider hides PO-token bindings while retaining cookie/visitor/DataSync, so BotGuard minting must launch the real headless Chromium provider.",
    "playback": "A real resolved remote stream is loaded into the real VlcjPlaybackController at volume 0; play/advance/seek/pause/resume/stop are asserted from PlaybackSnapshot."
